## c50ae84 ← d1e2739  (2026-09-22)

Added the thinking / reasoning knobs to the WebVoyager runner and a Claude
default config. `EVAL_ENABLE_THINKING=true` appends the fixed override
`--agent-kwargs '{"enable_thinking": true, "sampling_kwargs": {"max_new_tokens": 4096}}'`
and names the slug `think_on` / `think_xhigh`; `EVAL_REASONING_EFFORT` forwards
`--api-kwargs '{"reasoning_effort": …}'` for gpt-* and names the slug
`reasoning_<effort>`. Each variant therefore gets its own artifact dir and never
resumes another's, so rows are only comparable within one `EVAL_CONFIG_ID`.

## d1e2739  (2026-09-13)

Added WebVoyager default-config routing for Qwen3.8, UI-TARS-1.5, EvoCUA and
UI-Venus-2. Runs evaluate the 643-task read-only split via
`--filter 'lambda m: not m.others.get("mutating")'` with `--env-kwargs
'{"max_steps": 30}'`.

## 651af22040  (2026-07-10)

Default and SoM snapshots were materialized as separate run ids at this commit.
The aggregate `run_0_som.json` config-id mismatch is tracked separately by the
eval snapshot-integrity audit; it is not a metric-definition change.

The owner-resolved browser coord screenshot-only policy is not recorded here as
landed yet because its env/config change is pending Issue 1b. Add a commit-scoped
entry when that change lands.

## c1001a613c  (2026-07-08)

Initial standardized WebVoyager snapshot at this commit. Default and SoM modes
use separate config files under `scripts/configs/*/default/webharbor.webvoyager/`
and are not interchangeable rows in a results table.
